I'd taken a break of nearly a year in my ongoing goal of ascending
in all classes (now 6/13!), and then resumed playing healers.
This game seemed to be almost charmed.

On the way to doing the protection racket (with great success),
I found both an AoR and a BoH (I still did Sokoban, though, for
fun, food, and exercise), as well as several conveniently located
altars. Having a blessed BoH early on is a huge advantage. Did Sokoban,
returned to the Gnomish mines to finish them up, scoring a 
wish from a magic lamp that netted me the Eye of the Aethiopica.

Wielded elven daggers for a long time (oddly, I never found a quarterstaff
until the Staff in the quest, and never met a unicorn until after that)
until some holy water conversion at an altar also yielded Magicbane.
An obliging orange dragon got me ODSM. I found and id'd a blessed
scroll of charging. I got teleport control from a tengu. I later
had to seek out a nymph to get teleportitis to go with it.

Arrived at Medusa's island with no way to cross water or blind myself,
so I dug down, did the Castle via frontal assault (with the help of a
cockatrice that laid down its life for the statuary arts), grabbed the
/oW and found boots of levitation.

On the upstairs just below Medusa, I realized I had no means of
blinding myself. Just at that moment, a yellow light shows up,
and blinds me. I rush upstairs, and flash Medusa a look at herself.
Went back and did the Quest.

Perseus yielded nothing useful, but I found speed boots and a ring
of slow digestion elsewhere and was ready for Gehennom. Valley of the
Dead was a bones level, and a fellow player's Wizard ghost contributed
another /oW (1 charge left), a +5 robe, a GDSM, a ring of conflict,
a ring of levitation, and some handy spellbooks. Used the Eye to stash
a bunch of stuff in Sokoban and went back to harrow Hell.  Used the /oW
with the single charge to get a magic marker for later first, though.

Gehennom was essentially painless at that point. I had learned
magic mapping with 93% failure, but with the Eye doing magic regen,
I took the odds, and mapped every level. Orcus's wand of death did for
Rodney (twice), and the ring of conflict simplified Moloch's Sanctum
considerably. 

Raced up, only getting sent back a level once (so much easier than being
lawful) and stopped off at my Sokoban stash to switch to the inventory
I wanted for the Ascension run, write some scrolls (cursed genocide,
taming, charging), get things blessed, etc. While I'm doing that, and
thinking about wishing for SDSM so I can wear one of the two AoLS's
I picked up along the way (Vlad's and a random one), what happens? A
silver dragon is generated. I kill it, and it leaves scales. Voila.

Elemental planes: Earth (uneventful), Air (lots of teleporting out
of air elementals, a few scary moments), Fire (uneventful),
and Water (uneventful, and floated to the portal somewhat faster
than usual). 

Astral plane: Cursed genocide of silver dragons + scroll of taming,
and now I have a buffer to work with. Tried the left altar first
(Pestilence, meet wand of death), wrong one. Back to the middle
(one more Pestilence encounter), and to the center altar with the
help of wands of teleportation. It's the right one! 2 wishes
for dilithium crystals and one blow on a magic whistle later, 
and it's:

Goodbye javelin the Demigoddess...

